Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL (@ic-inorganic-course: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR
Nanda Kishore, IIT Guwahati. Inorganic Chemical Technology, NPTEL 103103218. [Official course](https://www.nptel.ac.in/courses/103103218) · [Complete syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/103103218.pdf).

Complete the whole public sequence and worked material, following feedstocks, manufacturing reactions, process flows, engineering questions, and useful inorganic products. Use the named gas, acid, alkali, fertiliser, and other inorganic families as connected applications of shared chemical principles. Reconstruct balances and alternatives rather than memorising a single flowsheet.

Official course identity, instructor, scope, and public syllabus were verified on 29 October 2026. The syllabus endpoint subsequently timed out through the browsing tool; full playback and every assessment were not inspected. Preserve the actual course run and component notices. Free educational access is distinguished from an open redistribution licence and from certification. All media remain external.

